(window.CLAYSIMS_TEXT = window.CLAYSIMS_TEXT || {})["en"] = {"launch":"Launch","method":"Method","speed":"Target speed","distance":"Distance","demo":"Watch the method","try":"Your turn: press when you would shoot","shoot":"Shoot","hit":"Hit! The target breaks.","behind":"Behind — the shot passed behind the target","ahead":"In front — the shot passed ahead of the target","perceived":"Lead you see at the decision","actual":"Actual lead at the shot","lab_note":"Slow motion, simplified physics for teaching. The shot slows down as it flies: on average about 330 m/s over 15 m, 300 m/s over 25 m and 255 m/s over 40 m (it leaves the barrel at about 360–430 m/s). It takes about 0.15 s from the decision to the shot (an average estimate). The ring marks the part of the pattern dense enough to break the target: a radius of about 33 cm at 15 m and 45 cm at 40 m. The muzzle is about 1 m from the eye. Distances along the target's line, the lead and the ring are to scale; the target is drawn larger than life so you can see it (about to scale where the lead is counted in target widths). The actual lead depends on the target's speed, distance and angle, the cartridge and the shooter.","unit_m":"m","unit_ft":"ft","unit_ms":"m/s","pair_report":"{term}: the 2nd target is released at the sound of the 1st shot","pair_sim":"{term}: both targets are released together","pair_rafale":"{term}: the 2nd target from the same trap, as soon as the trap has reloaded","listen":"Listen","no_shot":"No shot fired.","at_muzzle":"seen at the muzzle","compare":"Same target, four methods: the actual lead is the same, the lead you see is not","how_maintained":"The muzzles wait in front and the target closes the gap. Press Shoot when the gap looks right: the gun then moves at the target's speed and holds that lead.","how_swing":"The muzzles start behind the target and move faster than it. Press Shoot as the muzzles pass the front of the target: the gun keeps gaining during the delay, so the actual lead is bigger.","how_pullaway":"The muzzles move with the target first, then accelerate ahead. Press Shoot while the gun is still accelerating: the lead you see is smaller than the actual lead.","how_ambush":"The muzzles wait still at a point ahead. Press Shoot before the target reaches that point: the shot needs time, so a shot fired as the target arrives goes behind.","stop_gun":"Stop the gun at the trigger (a fault)","clay_widths":"target widths","unit_cm":"cm","unit_in":"in","anim_play":"Play","anim_replay":"Replay","anim_slow":"Slow motion","anim_marker":"with animation","anim_h_flight":"Watch how the target flies","anim_h_points":"Watch the three points","anim_h_eyes":"Watch where the eyes look","anim_h_stance":"Watch the stance","anim_h_pair":"Watch how a double is thrown","anim_h_lead":"Watch how the lead works","anim_h_mount":"Watch the gun mount","anim_h_follow":"Watch the follow-through","anim_h_call":"Watch the call and the release","anim_h_gunpos":"Watch the gun position","anim_h_misfire":"Watch what to do after a misfire","anim_w_flight":"Follow the whole flight: where the target comes from, where you see it clearly and where it goes.","anim_w_points":"The eyes wait at the pick-up point, the muzzles at the hold point; the target breaks at the break point.","anim_w_eyes":"Soft focus around the pick-up point, then hard focus on the front edge of the target.","anim_w_stance":"The front foot points at the break point; the body turns back to the hold point.","anim_w_pair":"Watch when the second target leaves: after the shot, together with the first, or from the same trap.","anim_w_lead":"Watch the gap between the muzzles and the target at the moment of the shot, then try it yourself.","anim_w_mount":"The muzzles move with the target first; the mount is finished as the shot comes.","anim_w_follow":"The gun keeps moving after the shot; stop it at the trigger and the shot goes behind.","anim_w_call":"The clock shows when the target leaves after the call or the referee's signal; a late target is a No Bird.","anim_w_gunpos":"In Sporting™ the stock stays below the line on the vest until the target appears.","anim_w_misfire":"After a misfire, stay put: gun closed and pointing down the range until the referee has checked it.","anim_unit_s":"s","anim_after_call":"after the call","anim_after_signal":"after the signal","anim_t_signal":"Sporting™: referee's signal","anim_t_late":"Late target","anim_t_manual":"Compak® Sporting: by hand","anim_t_sonopull":"Compak® Sporting: {term}","anim_t_early":"Gun up at the call","anim_s_in_time":"The target leaves {n} s after the signal: in time (the limit is {max} s).","anim_s_late":"The target leaves {n} s after the signal, later than {max} s: the referee calls “No Bird” and the target is thrown again.","anim_s_manual":"Released by hand: the target leaves {n} s after the call (allowed: 0 to {max} s).","anim_s_sonopull":"Sonopull: the microphone hears the call and the target leaves {n} s later, every time.","anim_s_gun_low":"Ready position: the stock touches the body below the line on the vest.","anim_s_gun_mount":"The target has appeared: only now does the gun come up to the shoulder.","anim_s_early":"Called with the gun already at the shoulder: the first time, a spoken warning and a yellow card.","anim_s_click":"Click: the gun did not fire.","anim_s_hold":"Stay where you are: gun closed and pointing down the range; do not open it or touch the safety.","anim_s_ref":"The referee examines the gun.","anim_s_repeat":"First malfunction of the round: the target is thrown again.","anim_stop":"Stop","anim_s_mount_ready":"Ready: the gun is low and the eyes wait for the target.","anim_s_move":"Move: the front hand starts the muzzles along the target's line.","anim_s_mount":"Mount: the stock comes up to the cheek and into the shoulder; the head stays still.","anim_s_shoot":"Shoot: the mount is finished as the shot comes.","anim_scale":"Only the shooter and the stand are to scale; the field and the target's flight are shortened.","anim_h_pattern":"Watch how the choke changes the pattern","anim_w_pattern":"A shot at a plate from 36.6 m (40 yards). Pick a choke: the tighter it is, the more shot lands in the 76 cm circle and the denser it is on the target in the centre.","anim_pattern_in":"In the 76 cm circle: ≈ {n}% of the shot","anim_pattern_load":"Simplified. 28 g of No. 7½ shot is about 370 pellets; the percentages are a guide for lead shot, and your gun and cartridge may give different ones. The target (110 mm) and the circle are to scale.","anim_h_miss":"Watch where the shot went","anim_w_miss":"What a coach standing behind the shooter sees: first where the shot went compared with the clay, then why. Switch the tabs.","anim_miss_behind":"Behind: the shot passed behind the target — not enough lead, or the gun slowed down or stopped. Very common on crossers.","anim_miss_front":"In front: too much lead, often after over-correcting. Many coaches like this miss: it shows the gun kept moving.","anim_miss_over":"Over: common on dropping targets, rabbits and incomers, and often linked to the head coming off the stock.","anim_miss_under":"Under: typical on rising targets that are still climbing at the shot.","anim_h_ties":"Watch how ties are broken","anim_w_ties":"Places 1–3: a shoot-off; below third: countback (in Compak® Sporting the same, from the 8th Compak to the 1st). The numbers are an example: 200 targets, 8 layouts of 25.","anim_ties_shooter":"Shooter","anim_ties_total":"Total","anim_ties_place":"Place","anim_ties_layout":"Layout","anim_ties_so":"Shoot-off (25)","anim_ties_sd":"Sudden death","anim_ties_cb0":"D and E both have 181 of 200: 5th place. Below third there is no shoot-off — countback decides the order on the score sheet.","anim_ties_cb_eq":"Layout {n}: {a} : {b} — level, look at the one before.","anim_ties_cb_win":"Layout {n}: {a} : {b} — {who} is listed higher. Both keep the same place: 5=.","anim_ties_so0":"A and B both have 192 of 200 — a tie for 1st place. A shoot-off decides it: a round of 25 targets.","anim_ties_so1":"Shoot-off: {a} : {b} — still level. Now sudden death: the first to miss is out.","anim_ties_sd_ok":"Target {n}: both hit.","anim_ties_sd_both":"Target {n}: both missed. They have shot the same number of targets, so nobody is out.","anim_ties_sd_out":"Target {n}: A hit, B missed — B is out. A takes 1st place.","anim_h_stock":"See how a stock is measured","anim_w_stock":"A coach or a gun fitter sets the stock dimensions; the numbers here are only a guide.","anim_stock_b_fit":"Fits","anim_stock_b_short":"Too short","anim_stock_b_long":"Too long","anim_stock_b_off":"Cast off","anim_stock_b_on":"Cast on","anim_stock_fit":"Length of pull is measured from the trigger to the middle of the butt pad. For adults it is often about 36–38 cm (14¼–15 in); many factory competition guns come at about 37.5 cm (14¾ in). This is only a guide.","anim_stock_short":"Too short: under recoil the thumb of the trigger hand may hit your nose, and recoil feels stronger.","anim_stock_long":"Too long: the stock catches on your clothes as you mount the gun and may land on the arm instead of the shoulder.","anim_stock_off":"Cast off: the stock bends slightly to the right, for a right-handed shooter, so that the eye sits exactly over the rib. It is a matter of a few millimetres; the drawing exaggerates it.","anim_stock_on":"Cast on: the stock bends to the left, for a left-handed shooter. Without the cast a shooter needs, a gun may keep shooting to one side.","anim_cheek":"cheek on the comb","anim_l_foot":"front foot","anim_l_body":"body","anim_h_hit":"Watch what happens to the clay","anim_w_hit":"The magnifier follows the clay from the shot: dust only, or a piece that breaks away.","anim_t_hit_dust":"Only dust","anim_t_hit_chip":"A visible piece","anim_hit_dust":"The edge of the pattern touches the clay: a puff of dust, but not one piece breaks away — the clay flies on whole.","anim_hit_chip":"The edge of the pattern touches the clay: one small piece breaks away and is clearly seen; the rest of the clay flies on.","anim_t_late_manual":"Compak® Sporting: late target (by hand)","anim_s_manual_late":"Released by hand: the target leaves {n} s after the call, later than {max} s: the referee calls “No Bird”.","anim_t_uncalled":"Target without a call","anim_t_uncalled_shot":"Target without a call: a shot","anim_s_uncalled":"The shooter has not called yet, but the target is already out. He does not shoot.","anim_s_uncalled_shot":"The target is out without a call. The shooter mounts late, fires — and misses.","anim_t_broken":"Broken at the launch","anim_s_broken":"The target leaves the trap already broken in two.","anim_s_broken_hit":"The shooter breaks the larger piece.","anim_t_nobird_shot":"A shot after “No Bird”","anim_s_nobird_shot":"The referee calls “No Bird”, but the shooter fires anyway."};
